  "notes": "{誇張|こちょう} means exaggeration — making something seem greater or more extreme than it actually is. Used as both a noun and a ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ verb.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {誇張|こちょう}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to exaggerate\n- {誇張|こちょう}なし⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧: without exaggeration\n- {誇張|こちょう}⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{過|す}ぎる→過ぎる：01219_sugiru⟧: to exaggerate too much\n- {誇張|こちょう}⟦{表現|ひょうげん}→表現：03584_hyougen⟧: hyperbole, exaggerated expression\n- {誇張|こちょう}⟦して→する：00392_suru⟧⟦{言|い}う→言う：00515_iu⟧: to say with exaggeration\n\nLITERARY TERM:\n{誇張法|こちょうほう} is the rhetorical device of hyperbole.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{大|おお}げさ→大げさ：19918_oogesa⟧: exaggerated, dramatic (na-adjective, more colloquial)\n- ⟦{言|い}い→言う：00515_iu⟧{過|す}ぎ: overstatement, saying too much\n- ⟦オーバー→オーバー：01529_oobaa⟧: over-the-top (casual loanword usage)\n\nREGISTER:\nSomewhat formal. In casual speech, ⟦{大|おお}げさ→大げさ：19918_oogesa⟧ is more common.",
